ring  based on different criteria  i think there is one option i can't  recall off the top of my head for  hierarchical clustering so it's just one  of those metrics i believe euclidean uh  by default and then there are also other  metrics based on patterns that you might  expect across studies or  um  basically uh scoring of different  categories but for higher hierarchical  clustering there's only one metric  that's used um when we employ that in  ipa explicitly  yeah got it  uh actually  last question looks like they just came  in  well  can we analyze ngs sequence data  directly in ipa or is it complementary  to  the kyogen clc workbench  so it is complementary to the workbench  um with ingenuity pathway analysis as  you saw today we could bring in a list  of genes with gain or law gain or loss  of function variants and more commonly  as you saw through the public data sets  the typical starting point in ipa would  not be  raw sequencing data or even quantified  expression in samples but rather  differential expression  right or study  yeah yeah i think the best way to uh  think of that is that your clc genomics  workbench is for your secondary analysis  which gets you to that differential  expression and then ipa takes it over to  take that differential expression and  we'll just use that term broadly it  could be you know protein expression you  know obviously mrna expression micro rna  et cetera um and uh and then analyze it  there in ipa so  with that we are at time  thank you so much um oh eric are you  still with me  oh never mind i we did answer this  question i thought we had a last minute  question but no we we uh we took care of  it so  with that i'm gonna say thank you and  goodbye to everybody that concludes  today's session bye
 

